<div class="import-course-name-guide">
	<div class="icng-section">
		<p class="icng-kicker">Workflow A</p>
		<h3 class="icng-title">New upload</h3>
		<p class="icng-lead">Create new <strong>Course Name</strong> records in batches. Each course name must be unique in the system.</p>
		<ol class="icng-steps">
			<li class="icng-step">
				<div class="icng-step-body"><strong>Download the template.</strong> Click <strong>Download CSV template</strong> for five sample rows (using real <strong>Rank</strong> and existing <strong>Course Name</strong> values for prerequisites when available). Use <strong>Download existing course names</strong> to avoid duplicates.</div>
			</li>
			<li class="icng-step">
				<div class="icng-step-body"><strong>Columns.</strong> <strong>Required:</strong> <code>course_name</code> (new title, becomes the document name), and at least one of <code>rank_1</code> … <code>rank_5</code> with valid <strong>Rank</strong> names (each cell → one <strong>Qualified Rank</strong> row). <strong>Optional:</strong> <code>mandatory_prerequisite_course_1</code> … <code>mandatory_prerequisite_course_5</code> with <strong>Course Name</strong> titles (each cell → one <strong>Mandatory Prerequisite Course</strong> row). If a prerequisite is not in the catalogue yet, the import creates a minimal <strong>Course Name</strong> for it using the same qualified ranks as the row that references it; if another row in the same file defines that course name, that row is saved first automatically. Leave unused columns blank. Also optional: <code>course_abbreviation</code>, <code>parent_course_name</code>, <code>course_frequency</code> (<code>Yearly</code>, <code>Quaterly</code>, <code>One-off</code>). Legacy: <code>prerequisite_1</code> … <code>prerequisite_5</code> or pipe-separated <code>ranks</code> / <code>mandatory_prerequisites</code> still work.</div>
			</li>
			<li class="icng-step">
				<div class="icng-step-body"><strong>Upload and submit.</strong> Choose <strong>— New CSV import —</strong>, <strong>Upload CSV</strong>, then fix any red rows (duplicate name in file or already in the database). Submit when all checks pass.</div>
			</li>
		</ol>
	</div>

	<div class="icng-section">
		<p class="icng-kicker">Workflow B</p>
		<h3 class="icng-title">Reload a batch</h3>
		<p class="icng-lead">After import, pick a batch from <strong>Import batch</strong> to review links, remove single rows, roll over to edit in the form, or delete the whole batch.</p>
		<ol class="icng-steps">
			<li class="icng-step">
				<div class="icng-step-body"><strong>Roll over.</strong> Unlocks every course in the batch so you can open <strong>Course Name</strong> and save changes. Before roll over, you can <strong>Remove</strong> individual locked rows from this page.</div>
			</li>
			<li class="icng-step">
				<div class="icng-step-body"><strong>Delete entire batch</strong> removes all courses in that import. Other documents linking to them may prevent deletion—resolve links first if you see errors.</div>
			</li>
		</ol>
	</div>
</div>
